  "title": "Missing protocol state checks allow deposit and withdraw operations when protocol is inactive",
  "severity": "medium",
  "validity": "valid",
  "quality": "sufficient",
  "user_handle": "anchabadze",
  "body": "## Description:\n\nThe protocol implements an emergency pause mechanism through the `onlyActiveProtocol` modifier that checks `clearingHouse.active` status before allowing critical operations. However, this protection is inconsistently applied across the codebase. While trading functions like `placeOrder`, `liquidate`, and `backstopLiquidate` properly use the `onlyActiveProtocol` modifier, all deposit and withdrawal functions lack this essential safety check.\n\nThe affected functions include:\n- `deposit(address account, uint256 amount)` in PerpManager\n- `withdraw(address account, uint256 amount)` in PerpManager  \n- `depositTo(address account, uint256 amount)` in PerpManager\n- `depositFromSpot(address account, uint256 amount)` in PerpManager\n- `withdrawToSpot(address account, uint256 amount)` in PerpManager\n- `deposit(address account, address token, uint256 amount)` in AccountManager\n- `withdraw(address account, address token, uint256 amount)` in AccountManager\n\nThis means users can continue moving funds in and out of the protocol even when administrators have intentionally paused it due to security concerns, bugs, or other critical issues.\n\n## Attack path:\n\n1. **Protocol vulnerability discovered**: A critical security issue is identified in the protocol\n\n2. **Admin attempts emergency pause**: Protocol administrators call `deactivateProtocol()` to pause trading operations and prevent further damage\n\n3. **Trading functions correctly blocked**: All trading operations (`placeOrder`, `liquidate`, etc.) properly revert with `ProtocolNotActive` error\n\n4. **Deposit/withdraw operations continue**: Malicious actors or uninformed users can still:\n   - Deposit funds into a compromised protocol via `deposit()` or `depositTo()`\n   - Withdraw funds during the pause via `withdraw()` or `withdrawToSpot()`\n   - Move funds between spot and perp accounts via `depositFromSpot()`\n\n5. **State inconsistency and damage amplification**: The continued movement of funds during the emergency pause can:\n   - Worsen the impact of the original vulnerability\n   - Create inconsistent protocol state that complicates recovery efforts\n\n## Impact:\n\n- **Ineffective emergency response**: The protocol's emergency pause mechanism fails to provide complete protection, undermining its primary safety purpose\n- **Increased vulnerability window**: Attackers have additional time to exploit vulnerabilities through fund movements even after trading is paused\n- **User fund risk**: New deposits can be lost if deposited into a protocol with known critical issues\n\n## Recommended Mitigation:\n\n### Option 1: Extend existing `onlyActiveProtocol` modifier\n\nApply the existing `onlyActiveProtocol` modifier to all deposit and withdrawal functions\n\n### Option 2: Separate modifiers for trading vs fund operations\n\nCreate two distinct control mechanisms:\n\n```solidity\nmodifier onlyActiveTradingProtocol() {\n    if (!StorageLib.loadClearingHouse().tradingActive) revert TradingNotActive();\n    _;\n}\n\nmodifier onlyActiveFundOperations() {\n    if (!StorageLib.loadClearingHouse().fundOperationsActive) revert FundOperationsNotActive();\n    _;\n}\n```\n\n### Option 3: Granular control with three separate modifiers (Compound style model)\n\nImplement fine-grained control for maximum flexibility:\n\n```solidity\nmodifier onlyActiveTradingProtocol() {\n    if (!StorageLib.loadClearingHouse().tradingActive) revert TradingNotActive();\n    _;\n}\n\nmodifier onlyActiveDeposits() {\n    if (!StorageLib.loadClearingHouse().depositsActive) revert DepositsNotActive();\n    _;\n}\n\nmodifier onlyActiveWithdrawals() {\n    if (!StorageLib.loadClearingHouse().withdrawalsActive) revert WithdrawalsNotActive();\n    _;\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add these imports in `PoCPerps.t.sol` file\n```solidity\nimport \"../../contracts/perps/types/Enums.sol\";\nimport \"../../contracts/perps/types/Structs.sol\";\n```\n\nAdd below in `PoCPerps` contract and run `forge test --mt test_DepositWithdrawVulnerabilityWhenProtocolInactive`\n```solidity\nfunction test_DepositWithdrawVulnerabilityWhenProtocolInactive() external {\n        address testUser = makeAddr(\"testUser\");\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1000e18;\n\n        // Step 1: Mint USDC to test user and approve transfers\n        _mintAndApprove(testUser, depositAmount * 5);\n\n        // Step 2: Verify normal functionality when protocol is active\n        vm.prank(testUser);\n        perpManager.deposit(testUser, depositAmount);\n\n        uint256 balanceAfterDeposit = perpManager.getFreeCollateralBalance(testUser);\n        assertEq(balanceAfterDeposit, depositAmount, \"Deposit should work when protocol is active\");\n\n        // Step 3: Deactivate protocol using admin\n        vm.prank(admin);\n        perpManager.deactivateProtocol();\n\n        // Step 4: Verify trading functions are properly blocked\n        PlaceOrderArgs memory orderArgs = PlaceOrderArgs({\n            subaccount: 0,\n            asset: ETH,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitPrice: 4000e18,\n            amount: 1e18,\n            baseDenominated: true,\n            tif: TiF.GTC,\n            expiryTime: 0,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            reduceOnly: false\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(testUser);\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSignature(\"ProtocolNotActive()\"));\n        perpManager.placeOrder(testUser, orderArgs);\n\n        // Step 5: Test vulnerable deposit functions - these should fail but don't\n        uint256 balanceBeforeVulnerableDeposit = perpManager.getFreeCollateralBalance(testUser);\n\n        // Test deposit() vulnerability\n        vm.prank(testUser);\n        perpManager.deposit(testUser, depositAmount);\n\n        uint256 balanceAfterVulnerableDeposit = perpManager.getFreeCollateralBalance(testUser);\n        assertEq(\n            balanceAfterVulnerableDeposit,\n            balanceBeforeVulnerableDeposit + depositAmount,\n            \"VULNERABILITY: deposit() works when protocol is inactive\"\n        );\n\n        // Step 6: Test withdraw vulnerability - this should also work when protocol is inactive\n        uint256 withdrawAmount = depositAmount / 2;\n\n        // Test withdraw() vulnerability\n        vm.prank(testUser);\n        perpManager.withdraw(testUser, withdrawAmount);\n\n        uint256 balanceAfterWithdraw = perpManager.getFreeCollateralBalance(testUser);\n        assertEq(\n            balanceAfterWithdraw,\n            balanceBeforeVulnerableDeposit + depositAmount - withdrawAmount,\n            \"VULNERABILITY: withdraw() works when protocol is inactive\"\n        );\n\n        // Step 7: Verify actual USDC balance changes occurred\n        assertTrue(usdc.balanceOf(address(perpManager)) > 0, \"Contract should hold deposited USDC\");\n\n        // The test has successfully proven the vulnerability:\n        // 1. Trading functions (placeOrder) are correctly blocked when protocol is inactive\n        // 2. But deposit/withdraw functions still work when protocol is inactive\n        // This is the core vulnerability!\n    }\n```",
